# Bot1 has Rest in Peace out by turn 1. Bot2's Pest Infestation (X = 1) makes two Pest tokens ("when this token dies, you
# gain 1 life"); the spell is a card, so it is exiled as it resolves. On turn 7 Bot1's Lightning Bolt destroys a Pest: a
# token would be put into a graveyard too, so it is exiled instead (CR 614.1a) and never dies - Bot2 gains nothing, where
# with no Rest in Peace it would gain 1 (the Dauthi Voidwalker token scenario is that control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Rest in Peace
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x2
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Forest
Pest Infestation
Forest x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rest in Peace.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#3.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Pest Infestation.Cast(X: 1)
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Pest)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T7 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 7
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Life = 20
Exile = Pest Infestation; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
